<%- include('../partials/header', { title: 'Business Audit Trail | NUCLEA' }) %><%- include('../partials/sidebar', { page }) %><div class="app-wrapper"><%- include('../partials/headbar') %><main class="app-main">
<div class="mb-4"><div class="text-primary fw-bold small text-uppercase">Governance / ALCOA+ support</div><h3 class="fw-bolder mb-1">Business Audit Trail</h3><p class="text-muted mb-0">Integrated business events: stock, BOM, batch parameters, QC results, signatures, labels, dispatch, GPS and POD.</p></div>
<div class="alert alert-warning small">Audit events are append-oriented at application level and this interface provides read-only display. Database administrators can still alter tables unless production database privileges, backups and tamper-evidence controls are separately configured; complete regulated audit-trail validation is still required.</div>
<div class="card"><div class="card-header"><strong>Latest 300 events</strong><span class="text-muted small"><%= events.length %> rows</span></div><div class="table-responsive"><table class="table table-hover align-middle mb-0"><thead><tr><th>Timestamp</th><th>Actor</th><th>Role</th><th>Action</th><th>Entity</th><th>Ref</th><th>Reason</th><th>Before / After</th></tr></thead><tbody><% if(!events.length){ %><tr><td colspan="8" class="text-muted text-center py-4">No events recorded yet.</td></tr><% } %><% events.forEach(e=>{ %><tr><td class="small"><%= new Date(e.occurred_at).toLocaleString('en-GB') %></td><td><%= e.actor_name||'—' %></td><td><%= e.actor_role||'—' %></td><td><span class="badge bg-light text-dark border"><%= e.action %></span></td><td><%= e.entity_type %></td><td><%= e.entity_id %></td><td class="small"><%= e.reason||'—' %></td><td><details><summary class="small">View JSON</summary><pre class="small bg-light p-2 mt-2" style="max-width:420px;white-space:pre-wrap"><%= JSON.stringify({before:e.before_data,after:e.after_data},null,2) %></pre></details></td></tr><% }) %></tbody></table></div></div>
</main></div><%- include('../partials/footer') %>
